@startuml processus
title 4+1 - Vue Processus (Runtime: threads, concurrence, IPC) - Conforme Kruchten

/'
**Vue Processus (Process View)** selon Philippe Kruchten (1995):

OBJECTIF: Montrer les aspects DYNAMIQUES du systeme a l'execution
- Decomposition en processus OS (dotnet, nginx, redis, mysqld...)
- Threads et pools de threads (ASP.NET ThreadPool, NGINX workers...)
- Mecanismes de concurrence (async/await, locks, queues)
- Communication inter-processus (IPC): TCP, HTTP, webhooks
- Synchronisation et ordonnancement

AUDIENCE: Integrateurs systeme, DevOps, architectes performance

IMPORTANT: 
- Cette vue montre le RUNTIME (processus + threads), pas l'architecture statique
- Complementaire a: Vue Logique (classes), Vue Deploiement (noeuds physiques)
- Etat initial = Monolith (UC-01/02 implementes)
- Etape 2a = Load Balancing + Cache + Observabilite (Phase 2 enonce)
- Etape 2b = Gateway + Microservices (Phase 2 enonce)
'/

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' =======================
' ETAT INITIAL: Monolith (avant Phase 2)
' =======================
package "Etat initial: Monolith - UC-01/02 implementes" {
  
  component "Processus 1: dotnet\n(BrokerX API)" as dotnet_proc {
    queue "ASP.NET ThreadPool\n(100-200 workers)" as threadpool
    agent "Request Thread 1" as t1
    agent "Request Thread 2" as t2
    agent "Request Thread N" as tN
    agent "Webhook Thread" as webhook_t
    
    threadpool ..> t1 : dispatch
    threadpool ..> t2 : dispatch
    threadpool ..> tN : dispatch
    threadpool ..> webhook_t : dispatch
  }
  
  database "Processus 2: mysqld\n(MySQL Server)" as mysql_proc {
    storage "Connection Pool\n(max 100)" as mysql_pool
  }
  
  component "Processus 3: otp-sim" as otp_sim
  component "Processus 4: kyc-sim" as kyc_sim
  component "Processus 5: pay-sim" as pay_sim
  
  ' IPC: HTTP appels synchrones/asynchrones
  t1 -[#1976D2]-> otp_sim : IPC: HTTP POST\n/otp/send (async)
  t2 -[#1976D2]-> kyc_sim : IPC: HTTP POST\n/kyc/verify (sync)
  tN -[#1976D2]-> pay_sim : IPC: HTTP POST\n/payment/deposit (async)
  
  ' IPC: Webhook callback asynchrone
  pay_sim .[#FF6F00].> webhook_t : IPC: HTTP POST\n/payment/webhook\n(callback async)
  
  ' IPC: TCP vers base de donnees
  threadpool -[#C62828]-> mysql_pool : IPC: TCP :3306\n(concurrent)
  
  note right of dotnet_proc
    Concurrence ASP.NET:
    - ThreadPool TPL (Task-based)
    - Async/await (non-blocking I/O)
    - PAS de locks applicatifs
    - Idempotency: unique constraint DB
  end note
  
  note bottom of mysql_proc
    MySQL concurrence:
    - Connection pool (max 100)
    - InnoDB row-level locking
    - MVCC (Multi-Version Concurrency)
  end note
}

' =======================
' ETAPE 2a: Load Balancing + Cache + Observabilite (Phase 2)
' =======================
package "Etape 2a: NGINX LB + Redis Cache + Observabilite (Phase 2 enonce)" {
  
  component "Processus: nginx\n(Load Balancer)" as nginx_proc {
    agent "Master Process" as nginx_master
    queue "4 Worker Processes" as nginx_workers
    nginx_master ..> nginx_workers : fork/manage
  }
  
  component "Processus: dotnet app-1" as app1 {
    queue "ThreadPool 1" as tp1
  }
  
  component "Processus: dotnet app-2" as app2 {
    queue "ThreadPool 2" as tp2
  }
  
  component "Processus: dotnet app-3" as app3 {
    queue "ThreadPool 3" as tp3
  }
  
  database "Processus: mysqld" as mysql2 {
    storage "Connection Pool" as mysql2_pool
  }
  
  component "Processus: redis-server\n(Cache)" as redis_proc {
    agent "Event Loop\n(single-threaded)" as redis_loop
  }
  
  component "Processus: prometheus\n(Metriques)" as prom_proc
  component "Processus: grafana-server\n(Dashboards)" as grafana_proc
  
  ' IPC: Load balancing round-robin
  nginx_workers -[#1976D2]-> app1 : IPC: TCP :8080\n(round-robin)
  nginx_workers -[#1976D2]-> app2 : IPC: TCP :8080
  nginx_workers -[#1976D2]-> app3 : IPC: TCP :8080
  
  ' IPC: Cache concurrent (GET/SET)
  tp1 -[#F57C00]-> redis_loop : IPC: TCP :6379\nGET/SET (concurrent)
  tp2 -[#F57C00]-> redis_loop
  tp3 -[#F57C00]-> redis_loop
  
  ' IPC: Base de donnees
  tp1 -[#C62828]-> mysql2_pool : IPC: TCP :3306
  tp2 -[#C62828]-> mysql2_pool
  tp3 -[#C62828]-> mysql2_pool
  
  ' IPC: Metriques (polling 15s)
  prom_proc .[#388E3C].> app1 : IPC: HTTP GET\n/metrics (poll 15s)
  prom_proc .[#388E3C].> app2
  prom_proc .[#388E3C].> app3
  
  ' IPC: Dashboards (PromQL queries)
  grafana_proc -[#7B1FA2]-> prom_proc : IPC: HTTP\n(PromQL queries)
  
  note right of nginx_proc
    NGINX concurrence:
    - Event-driven (epoll/kqueue)
    - 1 master + 4 workers
    - Chaque worker: 1000+ connexions
    - Algo: least_conn
  end note
  
  note bottom of redis_proc
    Redis concurrence:
    - Single-threaded (pas de locks!)
    - Event loop (epoll)
    - 50 000+ ops/sec sur 1 thread
    - Cache-aside pattern
    - TTL: 1-5 min
  end note
}

' =======================
' ETAPE 2b: Gateway + Microservices (Phase 2)
' =======================
package "Etape 2b: KrakenD Gateway + Microservices (Phase 2 enonce)" {
  
  component "Processus: krakend\n(API Gateway)" as krakend_proc {
    queue "Goroutines Pool\n(Go runtime)" as krakend_pool
  }
  
  component "Processus: orders-svc\n(Service Ordres)" as orders_proc
  component "Processus: portfolio-svc\n(Service Portefeuille)" as portfolio_proc
  component "Processus: reporting-svc\n(Service Rapports)" as reporting_proc
  component "Processus: auth-svc\n(Service Auth)" as auth_proc
  
  database "Processus: mysqld\n(orders DB)" as db_orders
  database "Processus: mysqld\n(portfolio DB)" as db_portfolio
  
  ' IPC: Gateway routing (HTTP)
  krakend_pool -[#1976D2]-> orders_proc : IPC: HTTP\n/api/v1/orders/*
  krakend_pool -[#1976D2]-> portfolio_proc : IPC: HTTP\n/api/v1/portfolios/*
  krakend_pool -[#1976D2]-> reporting_proc : IPC: HTTP\n/api/v1/reports/*
  krakend_pool -[#1976D2]-> auth_proc : IPC: HTTP\n/api/v1/auth/*
  
  ' IPC: DB par service (isolation)
  orders_proc -[#C62828]-> db_orders : IPC: TCP :3306
  portfolio_proc -[#C62828]-> db_portfolio : IPC: TCP :3306
  
  note right of krakend_proc
    KrakenD concurrence:
    - Goroutines = threads legers Go
    - 1000+ goroutines concurrentes
    - Circuit breaker par backend
    - Rate limiting: 100 req/s/endpoint
    - Aggregation de reponses
  end note
  
  note bottom of orders_proc
    Microservices:
    - Processus independants
    - DB dediee (isolation)
    - Scalable horizontalement
    - Communication via Gateway
  end note
}

' =======================
' LEGENDE
' =======================
legend bottom
  **Legende IPC (Inter-Process Communication)**:
  - Bleu (#1976D2): HTTP/TCP requests (sync/async)
  - Orange (#F57C00): Redis cache (GET/SET concurrent)
  - Rouge (#C62828): MySQL DB (connection pool)
  - Vert (#388E3C): Prometheus metrics (polling)
  - Violet (#7B1FA2): Grafana queries (PromQL)
  
  **Mecanismes de concurrence**:
  - ThreadPool: workers TPL .NET (Task Parallel Library)
  - Event Loop: single-threaded (Redis, NGINX event-driven)
  - Goroutines: lightweight threads Go (KrakenD)
  - Async/await: non-blocking I/O (.NET)
  
  **Progression Phase 2**:
  - Etat initial: Monolith (UC-01/02 implementes)
  - Etape 2a: Load Balancing + Cache + Observabilite
  - Etape 2b: Gateway + Microservices
  
  **Coherence avec autres vues 4+1**:
  - Vue Logique (logique.puml): classes et interfaces metier
  - Vue Deploiement (deploiement.puml): noeuds physiques et conteneurs
  - Vue Developpement (developpement.puml): projets .NET et dependances
  - Vue Scenarios (scenarios/*.puml): flux UC-01, UC-02, UC-03
end legend

@enduml
